swm on OpenRC
=============

swm runs as a user session, so no OpenRC system service is installed.
Enable seatd or elogind at the system level, then launch `/usr/bin/swm-session`
from your display manager or login shell (a D-Bus user session with
`dbus-update-activation-environment` is needed for portal activation).

`swm-session` checks for an active systemd user manager first and a configured
dinit user manager second; without either, it execs `swm --session` directly.
swm then publishes `WAYLAND_DISPLAY` and `XDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP=SWM` via
`dbus-update-activation-environment`.

Set `SWM_NO_INIT_INTEGRATION=1` to force the direct path even if a user service
manager is present.
